  "text": "\r\n\t Voting Information - Town of Gilford, NH \r\nTown of Gilford, NH \nDepartments \nAssessing Office \nBuilding Inspector - Code Enforcement Officer \nFinance Department \nFire-Rescue \nGilford Police Department \nGilford Public Library \nHealth Officer \nParks & Recreation Department \nPlanning and Land Use Department \nPublic Works Department \nTown Administrator \nTown Clerk - Tax Collector \nWelfare Office \nBoards & Commissions \nBoard of Fire Engineers \nBoard of Selectmen \nBudget Committee \nCapital Improvements Planning Committee \nCemetery Trustees  \nConservation Commission \nEnergy Committee \nGunstock Acres Village Water District \nHistoric District & Heritage Commission \nKimball Wildlife Forest Committee \nLibrary Trustees \nNEW GILFORD PUBLIC WORKS FACILITY PROJECT \nOld Home Day Committee \nPlanning Board \nRecreation Commission \nSite Study \nSupervisors of the Checklist \nTrustees of Trust Funds \nZoning Board of Adjustment \nTown Information \nAgendas & Minutes \nNews & Notices \nFiles & Documents \nOrdinances and Regulations \nPage Files \nPost Files \nRequest for Proposals \nStaff \nLinks of Interest \nAbout the Town of Gilford \nLive Meeting Viewer \nSpecial Events \nCommunity Power \nOnline Payments \nContact \nShow Menu \r\nVoting Information \r\nAbsentee Ballots Available \nNew Changes for Voters 2026 \r\nElection Laws \r\nVoter Information \r\n26_Absentee_Ballots_Announcement_State_General_.docx \r\nState General Election Sample Ballot 2026 \r\n2026 State Primary Election Results \n2026 General Election Absentee Ballot \nSecretary Scanlan Informs Voters of Annual Checklist Verification Process \n2026 Town Election Results \r\n2026 Second Session Election Results Minutes 03.10.2026 \r\nVoter Registration \r\nPLEASE CLICK HERE FOR VALUABLE INFORMATION FROM THE SECRETARY OF STATE'S OFFICE ON HOW TO REGISTER TO VOTE. \nRegistration: \r\nIf you are 17 years of age and will be 18 years by the next election, a citizen of the United States and a resident of Gilford you may fill out a voter registration card at the Office of Town Clerk-Tax Collector. The voter card is forwarded to the Supervisors of the Checklist who will then determine eligibility for addition to the voter checklist. Photo identification or affidavit required. Proof of age and citizenship may also be required. You may also register to vote on Election Day at the polling place. \r\nThe Supervisors of the Checklist also hold sessions in accordance with the requirements of state law. The sessions are held at the Gilford Town Hall. The law requires posting of those sessions in the local newspaper. \r\nSupervisors of the checklist: \r\nMary Villaume 603-527-4798 \nIrene Lachance 603-527-4798 \nMiriam A. York 603-527-4798 \nEach voter requesting an absentee ballot must complete their own application.   \r\nTo access the State of New Hampshire Voter Information Look-up (Absentee Ballot - Party - Polling Place) Click on the \"Voter Look-up\" URL address below:   \nAbsentee Ballot Request Form 2025 \n2024 Federal-State Election Results \nClick here for Voter Registration and Absentee Ballot Request Federal Post Card Application (FPCA) \r\nClick here for link to NH Secretary of State Election Webpage \r\nClick here for Federal Voting Assistance Program \r\n2024 Pres Primary Minutes \r\nMail Absentee Ballot request form to:  \nDanielle LaFond \nTown Clerk-Tax Collector \n47 Cherry Valley Road \nGilford, NH 03249  \nOr fax to (603)527-4719 \r\nOr Scan and email  signed  (no digital signatures allowed) application to:  dlafond@gilfordnh.gov \r\n Town Clerk - Tax Collector \n Residency Requirements \n Vehicle Registrations & Titles \n Real Estate  Tax Information \n Facilities Decals \n Voting Information \n Genealogy - Vital Record Info \n Official Town Records & Meeting Minutes \n Uniform Commercial Code UCC \n Dog Licenses \r\n\t\t\t\t  Home \r\n\t\t\t\t  Agendas & Minutes \r\n\t\t\t\t  News & Notices \r\n\t\t\t\t  Files & Forms \r\n\t\t\t\t  Town Calendar \r\n\t\t\t\t  Departments \r\n\t\t\t\t  Boards & Committees \r\n\t\t\t\t  Find it Fast \r\n\t\t\t\t  Search \r\nTown of Gilford, NH \n47 Cherry Valley Rd.\r\nGilford, NH 03249 \n(603) 527-4700 \nHome \nDepartments \nBoards & Commissions \nTown Information \nOnline Transactions \nContact \nCopyright© 2026 Town of Gilford, NH. All rights reserved.\r\nWebsite by  Legend Software \r\n ",
